WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.202
Workplace Desk: follow a meeting-room issue from report to resolution.

00:00:05.202 --> 00:00:11.631
Start as the client. Search, status filters, and pagination help find existing tickets.

00:00:11.631 --> 00:00:16.241
Report an issue. Required fields are checked before anything is saved.

00:00:16.241 --> 00:00:26.900
Choose a common issue, then add the location and symptoms.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.253
TKT-1050 is saved and automatically routed to the Technical department manager.

00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:37.550
The demo selector lets us switch roles. Next: the department manager.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:43.247
The manager chooses a technician from the same department.

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:47.593
Prakash now owns the work. The status changes to Pending Resolution.

00:00:47.593 --> 00:01:00.192
Switch to Prakash, the assigned technician, to add a progress update.

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:04.530
The update is saved in the ticket history, with the author and time.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:16.270
After the repair, the technician explains the fix before resolving the ticket.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.271
Resolved. The explanation remains visible alongside the earlier update.

00:01:20.271 --> 00:01:29.370
Back as the client, the completed ticket appears under Resolved tickets.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.959
The activity trail shows who created, assigned, and resolved the same ticket.

00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:40.461
One issue, three roles, and a complete history. Setup and tests are in the README.
